         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_tutorial"] = "Because you are playing the <b>Tutorial</b> game, you will notice that many of the ship\'s features are not yet included.  As you play, these features will gradually be added to the game.\n\nFor example, you cannot buy a larger engine until the <b>Planet Special</b> feature is introduced to the game, and this happens near the end of the tutorial.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_size_1"] = "You currently own a ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_size_2"] = "-ton ship.\n\nThis does not mean you can carry ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_size_3"] = " tons of cargo.  The ship\'s engine room, bridge, passenger seating area, crew living quarters, life support systems, and fuel tanks take up approximately ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_size_4"] = " tons.  The remaining ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_size_5"] = " tons can be used to haul cargo.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_larger"] = "You cannot buy or sell your ship whenever you feel like it.  The Traders\' Union strictly regulates the sale of all commercial ships.  This helps to maintain a trade balance between the planets and prevents the larger companies from monopolizing the market.\n\nBy virtue of being a member of the Traders\' Union, your name is automatically entered in a lottery.  If your name comes up, you will be given the chance to trade in your old ship and purchase a new, larger ship.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_fuel_tank_1"] = "The fuel tank size (fuel capacity) for your ship is ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_fuel_tank_2"] = " tons.  This is the maximum amount of fuel your ship can carry.\n\nThe advantage of a larger fuel tank is that if fuel prices are high on one planet, you can usually afford to wait until you reach another planet before filling up your tank.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_crew_1"] = "The number of employees you have depends on the size and model of your ship.\n\nYour company currently employs ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_crew_2"] = " crew members.  You must pay each employee a weekly salary of ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_crew_3"] = " kubars.\n\nYou will not be required to hire any additional employees until you purchase a larger ship.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_engine_1"] = "Your ship has a ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_engine_2"] = "-kuarp engine.  The higher the kuarp value, the faster your ship can travel.  This is an advantage if you are trying to beat another player to a planet in order to buy up all the best commodities.\n\nYou can roughly compute the time it will take to travel to a planet by dividing the total <b>distance</b> by the <b>engine speed</b>.\n\nYou can purchase a faster engine by going to <b>Pyke</b> and clicking on <b>Explore Planet</b>, then <b>Special</b>.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_passenger_1"] = "The number of passengers a ship can carry depends on its size and model.  The ship you own now can accommodate up to ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_passenger_2"] = " passengers.\n\nThe more you spend on passenger advertising, the more people will want to travel on your ship.  On the other hand, the more you charge for tickets, the fewer passengers you\'ll get.\n\nAt this time you have ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_passenger_3"] = " passenger(s) on your ship and ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_passenger_4"] = " passenger(s) waiting to buy tickets.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_cargo_1"] = "The amount of cargo your ship can carry depends on the size and model of your ship.\n\nThe ship you own now can hold up to ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_cargo_2"] = " tons of cargo.  That means you can buy up to ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_cargo_3"] = " tons of commodities and transport them to another planet.\n\nGenerally, the larger your ship, the more tons of cargo you can carry.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_fuel_use_1"] = "Every time you travel to a planet, your ship consumes between 2 and ";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_fuel_use_2"] = " tons of fuel.\n\nOn average, the longer the distance travelled and the larger the ship, the more fuel is used.\n\nIf you want to save fuel, a good idea is to travel to a nearby planet, rather than one on the other side of Kukubia.";
         this.strings["frm_ShipInfo_help"] = "The <b>Ship Info</b> screen provides you with details about your ship.\n\nJust click on the buttons to find out more about your ship, fuel tank, crew, engine, passenger capacity, cargo bay and fuel usage.";
